:INFO
Art. 17d Using vehicles on the road for the first time
1 Vehicles that are used on the road in Switzerland for the first time are those that are registered for use in Switzerland for the first time and whose use specified in their initial registration corresponds to their actual use by the end user.
2 First use on the road in a customs enclave in accordance with Article 3 paragraph 3 of the Customs Act of 18 March 2005 (CustA) and in Liechtenstein is deemed use on the road in Switzerland. Use on the road in a customs enclave in accordance with Article 3 paragraph 2 CustA, with the exception of Liechtenstein, is deemed use on the road abroad.
3 The following are not regarded used on the road for the first time:
a. vehicles registered for use abroad more than twelve months before the customs declaration in Switzerland; or
b. vehicles registered for use abroad more than six months but no more than 12 months before the customs declaration in Switzerland and which have covered 5000 km or more at the following times:
1. at the time of the customs declaration,
2. at the time of first registration for use if the number of kilometres covered was not recorded at the time of the customs declaration.
4 …
|

